// Title: UAC Bypass Using NTFS Reparse Point - File
// Sigma ID: 7fff6773-2baa-46de-a24a-b6eec1aba2d1
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-30 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects the pattern of UAC Bypass using NTFS reparse point and wusa.exe DLL hijacking (UACMe 36)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/hfiref0x/UACME
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_uac_bypass_ntfs_reparse_point.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath startswith "C:\\Users\\" and FolderPath endswith "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\api-ms-win-core-kernel32-legacy-l1.DLL"
